# records of a3a74a05205e8f34
# f1 = Late, f2 = Ahead
# `holder.run(late.next = ..)`: `run` is looked up in front of the arguments, so its getter makes an object of Late that finds no `next` yet. If the code behind the lookup ticked at the call, behind the store,
# the name would count as laid ahead of every object, and the getter would find what is not there. What a statement in front of the call lays is laid ahead.
# SINCE 11-04 (R257) THE CLOCK OF START SAYS OF NO NAME THAT IT IS LAID AHEAD: through a hole in it the read of such a name gave undefined where the type said a function, and the process died; the claim fired on no program that we are judged by. What this test told apart by `laid-ahead` it no longer tells.
# RUN: link members mechanisms=all
# CHECK: on-prototype L1 "next" function=f{{*}}
# RUN(NOT): link members mechanisms=all
# NOT-NOT: on-prototype L0 {{*}}laid-ahead

